From 6c350867ef6e1d8bd3b2b6a4afe9b3122cf966e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paulo Ricardo <contact@pauloricardo.dev>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:56:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] perf(mcp): optimize guardrail, observability and network
 path

- Cache list_projects responses in guardrail (30s TTL) to skip
  re-parsing and re-filtering on repeated calls
- Replace structuredClone with in-place mutation in
  applyPayloadPruning and filterListProjectsResult to cut memory
  allocation on large AST payloads
- Lower code_search_surgical default limit from 200 to 30 to reduce
  LLM context waste; max remains 200 when explicitly requested
- Add per-phase latency histograms and call counters to the gRPC
  guardrail (mcp_guardrail_duration_seconds, mcp_guardrail_calls_total)
- Add proper Prometheus histogram bucket support to both observability
  modules (app and knowledge-sync) with configurable buckets and
  standard _bucket{le=...}, _count, _sum exposition format
- Expose AgentGateway MCP port directly on loopback
  (MCP_DIRECT_PORT, default 8081) to bypass the Nginx hop for local
  MCP clients, reducing latency by ~1-2ms per call

All 87 existing tests pass (73 app + 14 knowledge-sync).
